 or just \"cuko\". Sometimes local people also eat the dish with yellow noodles and diced cucumber to balance out the vinegar's sourness, or adding chili powder to give the vinegar spiciness."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pempek"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pempek"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"],["Palembang cuisine","cuisine/palembang-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Flavor enhancer","ingredient/flavor-enhancer"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Tamarind","ingredient/tamarind"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d2/Pempek_lenjer_dan_krispi.jpg/500px-Pempek_lenjer_dan_krispi.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Pungkas nurrohman","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pempek_lenjer_dan_krispi.jpg"}},"ingredient/fermented-bean-paste":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/fermented-bean-paste","n":"Fermented bean paste","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Fermented bean paste is a category of fermented foods typically made from ground soybeans, which are indigenous to the cuisines of East, South and Southeast Asia. In some cases, such as the production of miso, other varieties of beans, such as broad beans, may also be used."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-fermented-bean-paste"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fermented_bean_paste"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Koryo-saram cuisine","cuisine/koryo-saram-cuisine",[["Pukjai","dish/pukjai"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Doenjang","ingredient/doenjang"],["Fermented soybean paste","ingredient/fermented-soybean-paste"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ee/Doenjangwithbeans.jpg/500px-Doenjangwithbeans.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Badagnani","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doenjangwithbeans.jpg"}},"dish/sate-lilit":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sate-lilit","n":"Sate lilit","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Sate lilit is a satay variant in Indonesia, originating from Balinese cuisine. This satay is made from minced pork, fish, chicken, beef, or even turtle meat, which is then mixed with grated coconut, thick coconut milk, lemon juice, shallots, and pepper. The spiced minced meat is wound around bamboo, sugar cane or lemongrass sticks, it is then grilled on charcoal. Unlike skewers of other satay recipes which is made narrow and sharp, the bamboo skewer of sate lilit is flat and wide. This wider surface allowed the minced meat to stick and settle. The term lilit in Balinese and Indonesian means \"to wrap around\", which corresponds to its making method to wrapping around instead of skewering the meat."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sate-lilit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sate_lilit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Balinese cuisine","cuisine/balinese-cuisine"],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":12,"links":[["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Grated coconut","ingredient/grated-coconut"],["Kencur","ingredient/kencur"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Pig","ingredient/pig"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Balinese cuisine","links":[["Plecing kangkung","dish/plecing-kangkung"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/0/0f/Satay_Lilit.jpg","w":500,"h":566,"by":"Flickr user: boo licious https://www.flickr.com/photos/71284893@N00/","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Satay_Lilit.jpg"}},"dish/shorshe-ilish":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/shorshe-ilish","n":"Shorshe ilish","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Bangladeshi cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Shorshe ilish is a Bengali dish, native to the Bengal region of South Asia, made from hilsa or Tenualosa ilisha, a type of herring, cooked in mustard gravy. The dish is popular among the people of Bangladesh. It is widely considered the national dish of Bangladesh. It is also popular in the Indian states of West Bengal, Tripura and Assam's Barak Valley."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-shorshe-ilish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shorshe_ilish"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Bangladeshi cuisine","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Hilsa","ingredient/hilsa"],["Ilish","ingredient/ilish"],["Mustard","ingredient/mustard"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Mustard oil","ingredient/mustard-oil"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"]]},{"h":"More from Bangladeshi cuisine","links":[["Chhanamukhi","dish/chhanamukhi"],["Durus kura","dish/durus-kura"],["Shemai","dish/shemai"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Zarda (food)","dish/zarda-food"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9a/%E0%A6%90%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%80_%E0%A6%B8%E0%A6%B0%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%B7%E0%A7%87_%E0%A6%87%E0%A6%B2%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B6.jpg/500px-%E0%A6%90%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%80_%E0%A6%B8%E0%A6%B0%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%B7%E0%A7%87_%E0%A6%87%E0%A6%B2%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B6.jpg","w":500,"h":599,"by":"রিজওয়ান আহমেদ","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A6%90%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%80_%E0%A6%B8%E0%A6%B0%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%B7%E0%A7%87_%E0%A6%87%E0%A6%B2%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B6.jpg"}}}